<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>The Factored Form of a Quadratic Expression and the x-intercepts
    of Its Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01924</md:content-id>
    <md:title>The Factored Form of a Quadratic Expression and the X-Intercepts of Its Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d888f675-5c48-481a-bafa-48bdcdd60680</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Consider two functions defined by <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
         and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>g</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent custom-question-number" start-value="1" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Consider the function defined by <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00002">Then, answer questions a–g, and create a table of values in which to
        enter the given x values and their outputs using the function.</para>

      <exercise id="fbf538bb-f2c6-4352-9d03-9245f6291f4a" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">

          <para id="para-00003">a. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">0</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_7e3b60e8-2698-4351-b519-0dbf05268d6c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">

          <para id="para-00006">b. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">-3</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_36eff251-576a-4a08-a292-23ebe6b0caed" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">

          <para id="para-00009">c. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">0</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="c7ec1749-f6a9-420d-b76f-5177b09b99d9" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">

          <para id="para-00012">d. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">5</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_4ead2d8e-cb7a-4723-884e-3f093a5cfd92" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">

          <para id="para-00015">e. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00016">12</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_3e2149b6-ffc9-4aa2-b353-5138c9cac85c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">

          <para id="para-00018">f. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00019">21</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="d7ee71b0-6b6c-47ba-9a7a-331832b8b0b4" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">

          <para id="para-00021">g. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00022">45</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

        <para id="para-00109" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">2. </span>Now, answer questions a–d to analyze the function defined by <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00024">a. What are the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-intercepts of the graph?
            Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00025">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00026">The <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-intercepts for function <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> are <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>. These
            points have an <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate that makes the
            output value 0.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->

      <exercise id="cd4fd094-81f0-44ce-bdc2-7c8ffd4a284c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">

          <para id="para-00027">b. What is the value of the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate in the vertex
            of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00028">-2</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="efc5a9b1-58bb-48f7-afa5-e4c45538c19e" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">

          <para id="para-00030">c. What is the value of the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate in the vertex
            of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00031">-4</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
          <para id="para-00033">d. What is the vertex of the graph of function <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>f</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>? Be prepared to show your
            reasoning.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00011">
          <para id="para-00034">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00035">The vertex appears to be at <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>. From
            the tables, the function values seem to change from decreasing to increasing at those
            points.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
        <para id="para-00110" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">3. </span>Consider the function defined by <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>g</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. Then, answer
          questions a–g, and create a table of values in which to enter the given x values and their
          outputs using the function. </para>

      <exercise id="e2b10c58-e3be-4468-b659-41230961de8d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00012">

          <para id="para-00036">a. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00012">
          <para id="para-00037">32</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_0ded0a1a-af60-483d-8d79-07df7ca15ea9" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00013">

          <para id="para-00039">b. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00013">
          <para id="para-00040">21</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_22c89b68-2f83-45e6-9397-cb6cccd55df5" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00014">

          <para id="para-00042">c. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00014">
          <para id="para-00043">0</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="fc365c44-9ee1-4f0b-b7f9-4e1165326aad" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00015">

          <para id="para-00045">d. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00015">
          <para id="para-00046">-3</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="dcbf8f49-f691-4ee2-b84d-5e96b1cfd5d4" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00016">

          <para id="para-00048">e. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00016">
          <para id="para-00049">-4</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_570ad872-751f-4c87-b55b-f71032c93d75" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00017">

          <para id="para-00051">f. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00017">
          <para id="para-00052">0</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_5b0b1aff-8af2-4e7b-9fdc-0c41da2f0930" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00018">

          <para id="para-00054">g. When the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00018">
          <para id="para-00055">5</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

        <para id="para-00111" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">4. </span>Now, answer questions a–d to analyze the function defined by <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>g</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00019">
          <para id="para-00057">a. What are the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-intercepts of the graph?
            Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00019">
          <para id="para-00058">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00059">The <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-intercepts for function <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> are <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>. These
            points have an <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate that makes the
            output value 0.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->

      <exercise id="_3192dc06-76cb-40d2-9e9b-1ead9c311094" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00020">

          <para id="para-00060">b. What is the value of the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate in the vertex
            of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00020">
          <para id="para-00061">2</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_94ee4a87-d64f-4f3a-ad32-31ba6177aa8b" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00021">

          <para id="para-00063">c. What is the value of the <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>-coordinate in the vertex
            of the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00021">
          <para id="para-00064">-4</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00022">
          <para id="para-00066">d. What is the vertex of the graph of function <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>? Be prepared to show your
            reasoning.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00022">
          <para id="para-00067">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00068">The vertex appears to be at <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>. From
            the tables, the function values seem to change from decreasing to increasing at those
            points.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
  

        <para id="para-00112" class="custom-question-container"><span class="custom-question-number">5. </span>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course.</para>
    <media alt="insert alt text">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media>
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00023">
          <para id="para-00069">a. Plot the points from the tables on the same coordinate plane.
            (Consider using different colors or markings for each set of points so you can tell them
            apart.)</para>
 
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00023">
          <para id="para-00071">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00072">
            <media alt="Coordinate grid with two graphs shown by plotted points.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_13_03_01.svg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00024">
          <para id="para-00073">b. Make a couple of observations about how the two graphs compare.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00024">
          <para id="para-00074">Compare your answer: </para>
          <list id="list-00006">
            <item>The <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-intercept of both
              graphs is at <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>.</item>
            <item>The graphs seem to be a reflection of each other across the <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-axis.</item>
            <item>The vertices both have a <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-coordinate of -4
              and also mirror one another across the <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>-axis.</item>
            <item>Each function mirrors itself across a vertical line through its vertex.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>

    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <exercise id="exer-00008">
        <problem id="prob-00026">
          <para id="para-00075"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_7_11_2_SC"/></para>
        </problem>
      </exercise>
    </note>

    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00006">
        <title>Determining Parts of a Graph from a Table</title>
        <para id="para-00076">Identify the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-intercepts and vertex of the
          quadratic from the table:</para>
        <table class="unnumbered os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
          <tgroup cols="6">
<tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis><m:math>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></emphasis></entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00077">-5</para>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00078">-3</para>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00079">-1</para>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00080">0</para>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00081">1</para>
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><emphasis><m:math>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:math></emphasis></entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00082">16</para>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00083">0</para>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00084">-2</para>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00085">0</para>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <para id="para-00086">16</para>
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table>

        <para id="para-00087">The <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-intercepts are where the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>y</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>-values are 0.</para>
        <para id="para-00088">This occurs at <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mo>,</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              <m:mo>,</m:mo>
              <m:mn>0</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00089">The vertex occurs where the function will create a mirror image, or be
          symmetrical for all points. This often occurs halfway between the two zeros (when there
          are two zeros).</para>
        <para id="para-00090">For this function, the vertex is at <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
              <m:mn>1</m:mn>
              <m:mo>,</m:mo>
              <m:mo>&#8722;</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title> Try It: Determining Parts of a Graph from a Table </title>
        <exercise id="exer-00007">
            <problem id="prob-00025">

              <para id="para-00091">Determine the vertex from the table:</para>

              <table class="unnumbered os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00002">
                <tgroup cols="7">
<tbody>
                    <row>
                      <entry><emphasis><m:math>
                            <m:mrow>
                              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                            </m:mrow>
                          </m:math></emphasis></entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00092">5</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00093">6</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00094">7</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00095">8</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00096">9</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00097">10</para>
                      </entry>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                      <entry><emphasis><m:math>
                            <m:mrow>
                              <m:mi>f</m:mi>
                              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                            </m:mrow>
                          </m:math></emphasis></entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00098">0</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00099">4</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00100">8</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00101">4</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00102">0</para>
                      </entry>
                      <entry>
                        <para id="para-00103">-2</para>
                      </entry>
                    </row>
                  </tbody>
                </tgroup>
              </table>


              <para id="para-00104"/>

            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00025">
              <para id="para-00105">Here is how to determine the vertex from the table:</para>

              <para id="para-00106">The zeros are located at <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          and <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>0</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>.
          The vertex will be halfway between the two zeros. This occurs at <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>.</para>

              <para id="para-00107">The point in the table at <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> is <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                    <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          .</para>

              <para id="para-00108">This is the vertex.</para>

            </solution>
          </exercise></note>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>